    "notes": "1. Company is in the technology/software industry. Total operating cost is constructed as the sum of Cost of revenue (Product, Service and other) and Operating expenses (R&D, Sales & Marketing, G&A). The supplementary segment table confirms this composition, showing Total Cost of revenue and Total Operating expenses summing to the difference between Total Revenue and Operating Income.\n2. Interest expense is taken from the supplementary table for 'Other Income (Expense), Net'. The sign convention is followed: the expense reduces income, so the positive number from the statement (parentheses indicate negative in the context of Other Income) is reported as a positive value.\n3. Taxes are the 'Provision for income taxes' from the primary statement.\n4. All other components of 'Other Income (Expense), Net' (e.g., interest income, investment gains/losses, foreign currency, other) are not mapped to the requested fields (total_revenue, total_operating_cost, net_income, taxes, interest_expenses) as they are non-operating items. Therefore, they are not included in the arrays.",
